          "optionExtraction": {
            "source": "inline_lower_option_lines",
            "status": "parsed",
            "imageTokenCount": 0,
            "nonEmptyOptionCount": 4
          },
          "parserWarnings": [],
          "explanation": "The position of protoxylem (and hence the maturation pattern of primary xylem) differs in dicot roots and stems and is a reliable distinguishing feature even in older material. In dicot roots protoxylem is exarch (towards the periphery of the stele), whereas in dicot stems protoxylem is endarch (towards the centre of the vascular bundle). Thus option (c) protoxylem is the correct choice for distinguishing a dicot root from a dicot stem. window.addEventListener(\"blur\",()=>{setTimeout(()=>{if(document.activeElement.tagName===\"IFRAME\"){FirebaseEventsViaWeb.onVideoPlayInTextDoc();}});},{once:false});",
