          "explanation": "In glycolysis, the conversion of 1,3-bisphosphoglyceric acid (1,3-BPG) to 3-phosphoglyceric acid (3-PGA) is an energy-yielding process because it results in the production of ATP. During this step, phosphoglycerate kinase catalyses the transfer of a phosphate group from 1,3-BPG to ADP, forming ATP and 3-PGA. This reaction is an example of substrate-level phosphorylation, where ATP is directly produced from the substrate (1,3-BPG). Thus, this is an energy-yielding process as ATP is produced.",
