          "explanation": "(a) is incorrect - adhering junctions (adhesion belts, desmosomes) primarily provide mechanical attachment between cells and to the extracellular matrix, not direct intercellular communication.(b) is correct - tight junctions (zonula occludens) seal adjacent epithelial cells, preventing paracellular leakage of substances across a tissue (e.g., intestinal epithelium).(c) is incorrect - cementing and strong mechanical attachment are mainly functions of desmosomes/adhering junctions rather than tight junctions.(d) is incorrect - gap junctions provide channels for direct transfer of ions and small molecules between adjacent cells and thus facilitate communication; they do not create gaps between cells. Hence option (b) is the correct statement.",
