          "explanation": "Zoos and botanical gardens: These are examples of ex-situ conservation. They involve the preservation of species outside their natural habitats. Here, animals and plants are provided with a controlled environment that mimics their natural surroundings as much as possible. These facilities play a crucial role in breeding programs, research, public education, and reintroducing species into the wild when conditions permit. Zoos: Focus on preserving and breeding animal species.Botanical gardens: Aim to conserve diverse plant species, including rare and endangered ones.",
