          "explanation": "B. Cut the DNA with sticky end: EcoRI is a restriction enzyme that produces sticky (cohesive) ends by cutting between the G and A in the sequence GAATTC. C. Recognises a specific palindromic sequence: EcoRI recognizes the palindromic sequence GAATTC, where the sequence reads the same in both directions. D. Cut the DNA between the base G and A where it encounters the DNA sequence 'GAATTC': This is the specific action of EcoRI, cutting the DNA between the G and A of the GAATTC sequence. A. Cut the DNA with blunt end: EcoRI cuts the DNA with sticky ends, not blunt ends. E. Exonuclease: EcoRI is not an exonuclease. It is a restriction endonuclease, which cuts DNA at specific sequences, rather than progressively trimming nucleotides from the ends.",
